A two-cluster Edge matrix that this scheduler accepts and whose steal rule works, and counters for what each cluster type
waits for while a core of the other type idles.

The matrix is built when the CPU driver calls ml_cpu_init_completed (ArmCpu, boot argument armcpu-edge=1). Without the
call every edge stays closed: no thread moves between the E cluster (three A510 cores) and the P cluster, in either
direction.

The matrix the board patch builds does not do what it says on this kernel:
- P -> E is closed for the fixed priority, foreground and user-initiated buckets and open for default and lower. The
  scheduler requires an edge to be at least as open for a higher bucket as for a lower one
  (sched_edge_config_verify_non_decreasing_qos_strictness; its searches stop at the first closed bucket), so the check
  fails.
- E -> P allows stealing without migration, for an idle P core to take E work. The steal search admits a cluster's
  threads only when the fixed priority bucket of that edge may migrate (scr_incoming_migration_allowed,
  sched_edge_pset_peek_steal_possible), so a P core never takes them.

Here P -> E is closed for every bucket, so a thread that prefers P runs on P. Opening it for the utility and background
buckets alone would fail the same check and would move no thread: those buckets prefer the E cluster
(sched_edge_default_preferred_pset, and nothing changes a thread group's preference without a performance controller),
placement starts at the preferred pset, so a P run queue holds no utility or background thread that prefers P, and an idle
E core already takes back the ones that prefer E through the foreign rebalance. E -> P allows stealing for every bucket
with the weight of a weighted spill (a steal then needs more runnable threads than E cores) and migration for the fixed
priority bucket alone, which opens the steal search and moves nothing: no thread group prefers E for that bucket.

Counters, each with index 0 for the E and 1 for the P cluster type: sheng_edge_cross_type_steals counts the threads a
cluster took from the run queues of the other type; sheng_edge_idle_beside_excess counts the times a core found nothing
to run while the other type had more runnable threads than cores; sheng_edge_idle_beside_queued splits the second by what
was queued there: per scheduling bucket the threads that prefer the other type (the ones the matrix keeps there), nothing
of that kind, and threads that prefer this core's type.

Applies after zzyf-sheng-amp.patch and zzzz-sheng-ipados27-bringup.patch. Has not run on hardware.
